To run:

1. Install eclipse IDE 

2. Import the entire Everything_09112014 folder in Eclipse

3. Compile and run (main file is EvaluateIt)

 - if display does not work, or seems stuck, try

   Thread.sleep(200); 

   instead of Thread.sleep(20); in Display.java (line 102)

4. To train, run the Driver class. 

5. Input mapping: 

  - the input neurons in the chromosome have the following order:

    input[0] = arm.theta1/90;		// arm angles
    input[1] = arm.theta2/90; 
    input[2] = r_d/260;			// distance to object
    input[3] = r_degree_theta / 90;	// angle to object	
    input[4] = r_d_pick/260;		// distance to tool handle
    input[5] = r_degree_pick/90;	// angle to tool handle
    input[6] = 0;			// arm limiter 1
    input[7] = 0;			// arm limiter 2

  - output : the two arm angles
